---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Banner Settings">
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Banner Settings</h1>

    <h2>Scheduler</h2>
    <p>Configure when your banner appears:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Permanent visibility</strong> - Always visible (default)</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Date range</strong> - You can set specific start and end dates and hours
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Start date:</strong> Select the day, month, year and hour when your banner should appear</li>
          <li><strong>End date:</strong> Select the day, month, year and hour when your banner should disappear</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-tip">
      <p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Schedule banners in advance for holiday sales, product launches, or time-limited promotions to automate your marketing campaigns.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Playback Options</h2>
    <p>Customize the way your banner is shown:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Auto-play</strong> - Enable/disable automatic slide change progression</li>
      <li><strong>Pause on hover</strong> - Enable/disable the option to stop the slide change when mouse hovers over the banner</li>
      <li><strong>Show navigation arrows</strong> - Toggle visibility of arrows for manual navigation</li>
      <li><strong>Show navigation dots</strong> - Toggle visibility of dots indicating slide position</li>
      <li><strong>Animation speed</strong> - Control how fast the animation plays</li>
      <li><strong>Animation type</strong> - Choose the style of slide transition</li>
      <li><strong>Slide interval</strong> - Define the time each slide is displayed before moving to the next one</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-note">
      <p><strong>Note:</strong> Choose animations that match your brand style. Subtle animations often perform better than flashy ones.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-tip">
      <h3>Recommended Settings</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Interval time:</strong> 5-7 seconds per slide gives users enough time to read content</li>
        <li><strong>Pause on hover:</strong> Enable this to let users control their viewing experience</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-play:</strong> Great for hero banners, but consider disabling for informational content</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Dimensions</h2>
    <p>Control how your banner dimensions are calculated. Banner dimensions are determined by several factors working together:</p>

    <h3>Default Dimension Factors</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Width:</strong> Defined by the target container you selected for your banner placement</li>
      <li><strong>Height (with images):</strong> Automatically set based on the uploaded image height for Image or Image and Text slides</li>
      <li><strong>Height (without images):</strong> Uses the "Banners maximum height" setting from the Theme section</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-info">
      <p>The <strong>"Banners maximum height"</strong> is a global setting found in the Theme section. It's an input field where you can set a fixed pixel value that applies to all banners in your store. You can change this value anytime to match your store's design requirements.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Height Override Modes</h3>
    <p>You can override the default dimension behavior by selecting one of these modes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Default</strong> - Uses the fixed height defined in "Banners maximum height" from the Theme section
        <ul>
          <li>Best for maintaining consistent banner heights across your entire store</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Percentage</strong> - Set the height as a percentage value relative to the container
        <ul>
          <li>Ideal for responsive designs that need to adapt to different container sizes</li>
          <li>Be careful to prevent pixelation - ensure your images have sufficient resolution to scale properly</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Full Window Height</strong> - Makes the banner occupy the full visible window height
        <ul>
          <li>Perfect for hero banners, landing pages, and immersive experiences</li>
          <li>Use sparingly as it can be overwhelming on mobile devices</li>
          <li>Always test on different screen sizes before publishing</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Custom</strong> - Specify an exact height value in pixels
        <ul>
          <li>Use when you need precise control for specific campaigns or design requirements</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-info">
      <h3>Best Practices</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Image consistency:</strong> Maintain consistent image resolution across all your banners. Use images with a constant height to ensure a uniform appearance throughout your different slides of the banner</li>
        <li><strong>Testing:</strong> Always preview your banners in different viewport sizes before publishing to ensure they look great everywhere</li>
        <li><strong>Performance:</strong> Large banner heights can impact page load perception and user experience - optimize your images and test loading times</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <div class="mt-12 flex gap-4">
      <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/docs/slide-types`} class="btn bg-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-300">
        ← Previous: Slide Types
      </a>
      <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/docs/placement`} class="btn btn-primary">
        Next: Banner Placement →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
